{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells","id":1167995,"title":"[2E] Wolf-Blooded - Losing Tells?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-15T12:50:01-08:00","id":1167995,"title":"[2E] Wolf-Blooded - Losing Tells?","content":"So on the latest game session one of my new player had Wolf-Blooded character. He has <i>Shadow Twin</i> Tell - but for story reasons - I killed his twin in Hisil when character switched realms. With dead twin - the Tell is useless. But then what to do with character? <b>As ST - should I made him 'evolve' and develop new Tell in place of 'lost' one?</b> If yes - maybe you can point some Tells thematically related to <i>Shadow Twin</i>, so development would be more 'logical'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T13:50:28-08:00","id":1168015,"title":"","content":"How did it die? It was a plot-scripted death? If not, just make the twin appear alive again next night like if nothing happened. Tells are weird that way and is a good mystery to throw at them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Better still, treat the twin as a spirit that was discorporated and will eventually reform next to its fetter, the PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T19:56:45-08:00","id":1168103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1168015#post1168015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did it die? It was a plot-scripted death?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Idigam ate him! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was an answer to PC's 'I just go to Shadow Realm to escape my imprisiment' plan. And to put <b>dread </b>in character - As I understand, you always feel your Shadow Twin, like organ you never had, yes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1168015#post1168015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, just make the twin appear alive again next night like if nothing happened. Tells are weird that way and is a good mystery to throw at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... maybe, but this seems a bit<i> too</i> weird in my POV then....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1168015#post1168015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Better still, treat the twin as a spirit that was discorporated and will eventually reform next to its fetter, the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS sounds interesting! &lt;Checks spirits rules&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 186</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated wounds explode into bursts of ephemera stylized to their natures. For example, a forest spirit dies in a hail of rapidly vanishing pine needles. The spirit isn\u2019t actually dead, though, merely returned to dormancy unless it has also run out of Essence. If it has even a single Essence point remaining, it reforms in a safe place (a Resonant location, usually), hibernating. Once it has regained Essence points equal to Corpus dots, it can spend an Essence point to reawaken. As the spirit can\u2019t act while hibernating, this means waiting for the one point of Essence a day that it receives for being in a suitable area to slowly build up to the spirit\u2019s Corpus \u2014 which means that more powerful spirits take longer to recover from being \u201ckilled.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>So here are questions to <i>Shadow Twin</i> Tell then:<br /> 1. <b>What stats will have Twin as spirit?</b> Just makes PCs Attributes in to average Power, Finesses and Resistance and go from there?<br /> 2. <b>How Wolf-Blooded can collect Essence for it's Shadow Twin?</b> WHAT kind of Essence should it be, of what Resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T20:21:09-08:00","id":1168108,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think you\u2019d need to stat up the Twin as an actual spirit, though. Just say it\u2019s a pseudo-spirit of some sort, with details just close enough for the story\u2019s needs. (In this case, discorporation)<br /> <br /> If stats are needed, I recommend Rank 1-2, since a human soul is apparently Rank 2 and a Shadow Twin doesn\u2019t sound like a \u2018whole\u2019 soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T20:49:24-08:00","id":1168110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1168108#post1168108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think you\u2019d need to stat up the Twin as an actual spirit, though. Just say it\u2019s a pseudo-spirit of some sort, with details just close enough for the story\u2019s needs. (In this case, discorporation)</div> </div> </div> </div>I still need Corpus rating of Twin - and by this, I need Resistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 186</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once it has regained Essence points equal to Corpus dots, it can spend an Essence point to reawaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:25:31-08:00","id":1168116,"title":"","content":"I still prefer saying that you could just have the Twin reform at a dramatically appropriate time, rather than a fixed interval. <br /> <br /> Or just use derive its Resistance from the Wolf-Blood\u2019s stats in whatever way you like, cap it to the limit for Rank 1 or 2, and voila.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T23:21:51-08:00","id":1168133,"title":"","content":"Or the Void, that is in existence now makes the character a Waystone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T05:53:16-08:00","id":1168160,"title":"","content":"Since it's a twin linked to the Wolf-Blooded character, just use the character's Health as Corpus, if you don't want to just have the twin show up when it's dramatically appropriate like 21C Hermit suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T11:03:44-08:00","id":1168404,"title":"","content":"I'm with Tessie, they are twins after all so it makes sense that they have similar capabilities (Corpus=Health)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T00:00:46-08:00","id":1169838,"title":"","content":"Sanctity of Merits, tell is represented by a Merit (or at least additional ones are) so let them chose another or allocate merit dots to something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T00:25:32-08:00","id":1169839,"title":"","content":"Okay, I will go with Health = Corpus route, to make player wait sometime for reemerging of his Shadow Twin. Till this day I describe the feeling as missing the limb - limb that is not on your body, but much more, in your soul. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I will mark each day slowly return of 'feeling the limb'. as Essence will build up in PC.<br /> But we still do not have answer to second question...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1168103#post1168103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>How Wolf-Blooded can collect Essence for it's Shadow Twin?</b> WHAT kind of Essence should it be, of what Resonance?</div> </div> </div> </div>How Shadow Twin can collect Essence? What kind of Essence should it be? There are no 'Wolf-Blooded Essence' in game world that I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-23-2017, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T00:48:18-08:00","id":1169841,"title":"","content":"All the Essence created by its twin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T06:07:51-08:00","id":1169898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1169841#post1169841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Essence created by its twin.</div> </div> </div> </div>But WHEN Wolf-Blooded would create Essence? If we do not have Resonance, how can I judge Essence is created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T06:33:40-08:00","id":1169905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1169898#post1169898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But WHEN Wolf-Blooded would create Essence? If we do not have Resonance, how can I judge Essence is created?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance is not dependent upon specific spirits existing for it to exist and wolf--blooded are not subject to any special rules about their actions having spiritual consequences. If the character experiences strong emotions or perceptibly aligns themself with a concept, that's going to make ripples in the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:17:48-08:00","id":1185995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells#post1167995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on the latest game session one of my new player had Wolf-Blooded character. He has <i>Shadow Twin</i> Tell - but for story reasons - I killed his twin in Hisil when character switched realms. With dead twin - the Tell is useless. But then what to do with character? <b>As ST - should I made him 'evolve' and develop new Tell in place of 'lost' one?</b> If yes - maybe you can point some Tells thematically related to <i>Shadow Twin</i>, so development would be more 'logical'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of this is an issue with how you chose to deal with the Gauntlet and this Tell.<br /> Even if PCs enter the Shadow through the Gauntlet at the same point (a reflective surface, Waystone Wolf-Blooded, or a locus), the PCs are not guaranteed to actually make it through at the same place or even the same time, or even at all. Your player's Shadow Twin isn't necessarily going to poof into the realm imprisoned, regardless of your PC being imprisoned. It isn't like a multiple personality. They don't share the same space. It could happen, if your Shadow Twin were constantly being tugged around to the approximate places in the Shadow, but that would be a failure of the game mechanics if your PC (not in the Shadow) were to accidentally waltz their Shadow Twin into the maw of a particularly nasty spirit, completely without player awareness. As such, it is ST's responsibility to think of these things in light of an absence of rules related to the Shadow Twin tell.<br /> <br /> Given that there is a missing Shadow Twin that has discorporated, a Waystone tell may be appropriate until their Shadow Twin regains Corpus, in addition to perhaps awarding a bonus tell to bleed an Essence (or Willpower) that only the Shadow Twin recognizes and can feed off of, until the Shadow Twin reforms. Consider the Open Condition as well. With these two tells and condition, it will create a disincentive to use their Shadow Twin as a punching bag as without their Shadow Twin's Corpus, the PC's life will become a living hell dealing with spirits looking for a free ride. Additionally, they may end up stuck in the Shadow, or &quot;Caught&quot; in the Gauntlet, and unsure in some cases of how to return.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T10:29:18-08:00","id":1186000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1167995-2e-wolf-blooded-losing-tells?p=1169898#post1169898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But WHEN Wolf-Blooded would create Essence? If we do not have Resonance, how can I judge Essence is created?</div> </div> </div> </div>Third Nipple Tell, in addition to highly emotional or catastrophic concepts put into action. Since a twin is essentially (see what I did there), very much like yourself, the essence you naturally resonate is very much the essence your twin would benefit most from and seek out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","user":"TriCitiesLodge","date":". 02-14-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13347-tricitieslodge","name":"TriCitiesLodge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13347_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}